    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d240">

                <pb facs="0448" n="438" xml:id="pg438"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 8.</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Hammond to Mr.
                        Waddington.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-12-12"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 12, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I am directed by Earl Russell to transmit
                    to you herewith, to be laid before Secretary Sir George Grey, copies of papers,
                    as marked in the margin,<anchor n="*" xml:id="d240-f1"/> respecting the
                    enlistment at Queenstown of various British subjects to serve on board the
                    United States steam vessel-of-war the Kearsarge.</p>
                <p>The law officers are of opinion that the men who so enlisted on board the
                    Kearsarge should be prosecuted;under the foreign enlistment act; and Lord
                    Russell directs me to say that he is of opinion that such prosecution should be
                    instituted as soon as sufficient evidence is collected to sustain it.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. HAMMOND.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
